{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611262020410b3ed7f10f5f445f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a substantial task. Let me digest the ruling:\n\n**The defect**: On JS (Node), the Clojure frontend reads `1.0`, `0.0`, `1e0` etc. via `cljs.tools.reader` which returns a bare JS Number — kind is lost (integer vs float indistinguishable). On JVM, `clojure.tools.reader` returns `Double` for `1.0` — kind intact. So identical source text compiles to different Data (integer on Node, float on JVM) → different canonical addresses, different semantics.\n\n**The fix (option b)**: frontend-owned lexical preservation — a token-aware source reading stage for the Clojure frontend that retains numeric token kind and materializes Jing float64 Data for float literals. Plus:\n- Carrier admission in the forms compiler (`literal?`/`constant-form?` must recognize Float64 carrier).\n- Execution reboxing: portable profile routes floating ops carrier-aware.\n- Revision bump: new Clojure frontend revision + lowering/support profile (currently `c1-2` / `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1`).\n- Docs placements per RULING 4.\n- Re-pin per RULING 5.\n\n**The seven acceptance gates** (from RULING 5):\n1. Real source, not only hand-boxed fixtures — identical strings on JVM and Node through frontend source entry + REPL/catalog route. Cover 0.0, 1.0, -1.0, 1e0, 1.5, -0.0, integral floats at/beyond 2^53, small positive float rounding to zero; integer controls; preserve refusal for M/ratio categories.\n2. Structural preservation — top-level, binding/argument, vector, quoted/nested data, dynamic collection, metadata; repeated equal-valued tokens at distinct positions; comments/strings/chars/discarded forms with numeric-looking text not rewritten; macro-generated numeric Data; host map/set construction can't discard occurrence; float keys refusal on both hosts.\n3. Restore the corpus honestly — restore integral floats to