{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_0f1665d95a094f2aa3722881","type":"tool_result","content":"255\t\n256\t(defn validate-ast-call-sites!\n257\t  \"Validate the C1 claim of a produced map AST `ast` under `origin`:\n258\t   project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n259\t   canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n260\t   table. The projected table is a declared canonical table, so it is\n261\t   validated strictly (`:declared? true`). Returns true when the sets\n262\t   are equal.\"\n263\t  [ast origin]\n264\t  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n265\t        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n266\t    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin\n267\t                                  {:declared? true})))\n268\t\n269\t\n270\t(defn literal?\n271\t  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n272\t  [form]\n273\t  (or (number? form)\n274\t      (string? form)\n275\t      (true? form)\n276\t      (false? form)\n277\t      (nil? form)\n278\t      (keyword? form)\n279\t      (vector? form)\n280\t      (set? form)\n281\t      (map? form)))\n282\t\n283\t\n284\t(defn constant-form?\n285\t  \"True when compiling `form` yields a fixed value independent of the\n286\t   environment: scalars, quoted forms, and collections built entirely from\n287\t   constants. A symbol is never constant (it is a variable reference). A\n288\t   `quote` counts as constant only at the top level: nested inside a\n289\t   collection it must reach compile-form so the quote is stripped and the\n290\t   inner form evaluated as data.\"\n291\t  ([form] (constant-form? form true))\n292\t  ([form top-level?]\n293\t   (cond\n294\t     (or (nil? form) (number? form) (string? form)\n295\t         (true? form) (false? form) (keyword? form)) true\n296\t     (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) true\n297\t     (seq? form) (and top-level? (= 2 (count form)) (= 'quote (first form)))\n298\t     (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (every? #(constant-form? % false) form)\n299\t     (map? form) (and (every? #(constant-form? % false) (keys form))\n300\t                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n301\t     :else false)))\n302\t\n303\t\n304\t(defn- content-root\n305\t  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\n306\t   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\n307\t   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\n308\t   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\n309\t   root or ordering table.\"\n310\t  [ast]\n311\t  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n312\t\n313\t\n314\t(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n315\t  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n316\t   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n317\t   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n318\t\n319\t   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n320\t   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n321\t   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\n322\t\n323\t   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\n324\t   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\n325\t   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\n326\t   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\n327\t   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\n328\t   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\n329\t   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\n330\t   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\n331\t   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\n332\t   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\n333\t   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\n334\t   vector retains its written element order.\"\n335\t  [form tail? env macro-env]\n336\t  (let [ctor (cond\n337\t               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n338\t               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n339\t               :else ['assoc {}])\n340\t        [op seed] ctor\n341\t        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\n342\t        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\n343\t        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\n344\t        sorted-children\n345\t        (cond\n346\t          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\n347\t          (map? form)\n348\t          {:order :canonical\n349\t           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\n350\t                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\n351\t                                  cv (compile-child v)]\n352\t                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\n353\t                               :children [ck cv]}))\n354\t                          (keys form) (vals form))}\n355\t          :else\n356\t          {:order :canonical\n357\t           :records (mapv (fn [e]\n358\t                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\n359\t                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\n360\t                               :children [ce]}))\n361\t                          form)})\n362\t        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\n363\t                   :written (:children sorted-children)\n364\t                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\n365\t                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\n366\t                                  (:records sorted-children))))\n367\t        ;; A source assoc can shadow normal calls without capturing the\n368\t        ;; compiler's map constructors (including exception payloads).\n369\t        shadowed-map? (and (::outcomes env) (= op 'assoc)\n370\t                           (or (contains? (::defined env) op)\n371\t                               (contains? (::locals env) op)))\n372\t        call (if shadowed-map?\n373\t               (u/app (u/v 'clj/construct-map)\n374\t                      (apply u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) operands))\n375\t               (apply u/app (u/v op) (u/lit seed) operands))]\n376\t    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n377\t\n378\t\n379\t(def initial-macro-env\n380\t  \"Compile-time map of macro names known before any defmacro: none. The\n381\t   standard forms live in the expander's store, not here.\"\n382\t  {})\n383\t\n384\t\n385\t(defn- shadow-macro-env\n386\t  \"Remove shadowed names from the macro environment.\"\n387\t  [macro-env names]\n388\t  (apply dissoc macro-env names))\n389\t\n390\t\n391\t(defn- strip-symbol-meta\n392\t  \"Return an equal symbol without reader metadata.\"\n393\t  [sym]\n394\t  (if (namespace sym)\n395\t    (symbol (namespace sym) (name sym))\n396\t    (symbol (name sym))))\n397\t\n398\t\n399\t(defn- body-expression\n400\t  [body-forms]\n401\t  (cond\n402\t    (empty? body-forms) nil\n403\t    (= 1 (count body-forms)) (first body-forms)\n404\t    :else (cons 'do body-forms)))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"2e03bf45-bb11-47c5-937b-11647d0c30b6","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:21:10.441Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc","content":"\n(defn validate-ast-call-sites!\n  \"Validate the C1 claim of a produced map AST `ast` under `origin`:\n   project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n   canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n   table. The projected table is a declared canonical table, so it is\n   validated strictly (`:declared? true`). Returns true when the sets\n   are equal.\"\n  [ast origin]\n  (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin\n                                  {:declared? true})))\n\n\n(defn literal?\n  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n  [form]\n  (or (number? form)\n      (string? form)\n      (true? form)\n      (false? form)\n      (nil? form)\n      (keyword? form)\n      (vector? form)\n      (set? form)\n      (map? form)))\n\n\n(defn constant-form?\n  \"True when compiling `form` yields a fixed value independent of the\n   environment: scalars, quoted forms, and collections built entirely from\n   constants. A symbol is never constant (it is a variable reference). A\n   `quote` counts as constant only at the top level: nested inside a\n   collection it must reach compile-form so the quote is stripped and the\n   inner form evaluated as data.\"\n  ([form] (constant-form? form true))\n  ([form top-level?]\n   (cond\n     (or (nil? form) (number? form) (string? form)\n         (true? form) (false? form) (keyword? form)) true\n     (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) true\n     (seq? form) (and top-level? (= 2 (count form)) (= 'quote (first form)))\n     (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (every? #(constant-form? % false) form)\n     (map? form) (and (every? #(constant-form? % false) (keys form))\n                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n     :else false)))\n\n\n(defn- content-root\n  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\n   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\n   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\n   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\n   root or ordering table.\"\n  [ast]\n  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n\n   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\n\n   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\n   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\n   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\n   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\n   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\n   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\n   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\n   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\n   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\n   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\n   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\n   vector retains its written element order.\"\n  [form tail? env macro-env]\n  (let [ctor (cond\n               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n               :else ['assoc {}])\n        [op seed] ctor\n        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\n        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\n        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\n        sorted-children\n        (cond\n          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\n          (map? form)\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\n                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\n                                  cv (compile-child v)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\n                               :children [ck cv]}))\n                          (keys form) (vals form))}\n          :else\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [e]\n                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\n                               :children [ce]}))\n                          form)})\n        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\n                   :written (:children sorted-children)\n                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\n                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\n                                  (:records sorted-children))))\n        ;; A source assoc can shadow normal calls without capturing the\n        ;; compiler's map constructors (including exception payloads).\n        shadowed-map? (and (::outcomes env) (= op 'assoc)\n                           (or (contains? (::defined env) op)\n                               (contains? (::locals env) op)))\n        call (if shadowed-map?\n               (u/app (u/v 'clj/construct-map)\n                      (apply u/app (u/v 'conj) (u/lit []) operands))\n               (apply u/app (u/v op) (u/lit seed) operands))]\n    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(def initial-macro-env\n  \"Compile-time map of macro names known before any defmacro: none. The\n   standard forms live in the expander's store, not here.\"\n  {})\n\n\n(defn- shadow-macro-env\n  \"Remove shadowed names from the macro environment.\"\n  [macro-env names]\n  (apply dissoc macro-env names))\n\n\n(defn- strip-symbol-meta\n  \"Return an equal symbol without reader metadata.\"\n  [sym]\n  (if (namespace sym)\n    (symbol (namespace sym) (name sym))\n    (symbol (name sym))))\n\n\n(defn- body-expression\n  [body-forms]\n  (cond\n    (empty? body-forms) nil\n    (= 1 (count body-forms)) (first body-forms)\n    :else (cons 'do body-forms)))","numLines":150,"startLine":255,"totalLines":2253}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_0f1665d95a094f2aa3722881","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
