{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1bcb507731e14720933179e8","type":"tool_result","content":"2395\t\n2396\t(defn- usable-binding\n2397\t  \"The binding of a successful `selected`, when it has a parse and a lower\n2398\t   stage, else nil.\"\n2399\t  [selected]\n2400\t  (let [binding (when (frontend/ok? selected) (:binding selected))]\n2401\t    (when (and (map? binding) (fn? (:parse binding)) (fn? (:lower binding)))\n2402\t      binding)))\n2403\t\n2404\t\n2405\t(defn- frontend-binding\n2406\t  \"The installed binding for `lang` in the session's pinned catalog.  With\n2407\t   no parse and lower stage installed it throws an `unavailable-parser`\n2408\t   diagnostic: there is no fallback to another frontend.\"\n2409\t  [state lang]\n2410\t  (let [selected (select-frontend (:frontends state) lang)]\n2411\t    (or (usable-binding selected)\n2412\t        (throw (ex-info (str \"unavailable-parser: no parser for \" (pr-str lang))\n2413\t                        {:diagnostic :unavailable-parser\n2414\t                         :lang lang\n2415\t                         :selection selected})))))\n2416\t\n2417\t\n2418\t(defn- lower-parsed\n2419\t  \"Lower `parsed` through `binding`.  A binding with a `:lower-session`\n2420\t   stage lowers against the frontend session the shell keeps\n2421\t   (`:frontend-session`, cleared with the VM) and leaves the session it\n2422\t   answers, with the binding's `:render`, in the program's\n2423\t   `::frontend` metadata, for `eval-compiled` to stage.\"\n2424\t  [state binding parsed]\n2425\t  (let [lower-session (:lower-session binding)\n2426\t        [ast session] (if lower-session\n2427\t                        (lower-session parsed (:frontend-session state))\n2428\t                        [((:lower binding) parsed) nil])\n2429\t        staged (cond-> {}\n2430\t                 (:render binding) (assoc :render (:render binding))\n2431\t                 lower-session (assoc :session session)\n2432\t                 (:derive binding) (assoc :derivation ((:derive binding) parsed ast)))]\n2433\t    (cond-> ast\n2434\t      (seq staged) (vary-meta assoc ::frontend staged))))\n2435\t\n2436\t\n2437\t(defn- compile-input\n2438\t  \"Lower `input` through the selected frontend; `forms` are the shell\n2439\t   reader's forms, used by a frontend that consumes them.\"\n2440\t  [state input forms]\n2441\t  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n2442\t    (lower-parsed state binding\n2443\t                  ((:parse binding)\n2444\t                   (if (= :forms (:input binding)) forms input)))))\n2445\t\n2446\t\n2447\t(defn- forms-input?\n2448\t  [state]\n2449\t  (= :forms (:input (frontend-binding state (:lang state)))))\n2450\t\n2451\t\n2452\t(defn- compile-source\n2453\t  [state input]\n2454\t  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n2455\t    (lower-parsed state binding\n2456\t                  ((:parse binding)\n2457\t                   (if (= :forms (:input binding)) (read-forms input) input)))))\n2458\t\n2459\t\n2460\t(defn- compile-command-ast\n2461\t  \"The AST `(compile ...)` previews.  It lowers against a primed frontend\n2462\t   session: a session-staged frontend carries its prelude only on the\n2463\t   session's first lowering, and the preview is of the submitted form, not\n2464\t   of the runtime it would run on.  The session itself is not touched.\"\n2465\t  [state arg]\n2466\t  (let [state (assoc state :frontend-session :primed)]\n2467\t    (cond\n2468\t      (string? arg) (compile-source state arg)\n2469\t      (forms-input? state) (compile-input state nil [arg])\n2470\t      :else (throw (ex-info \"This compile command expects a source string\"\n2471\t                            {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n2472\t\n2473\t\n2474\t(defn- render-compile-output"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"4c7eeebf-f4c7-4058-b0b7-9c3323473216","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:21:24.781Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc","content":"\n(defn- usable-binding\n  \"The binding of a successful `selected`, when it has a parse and a lower\n   stage, else nil.\"\n  [selected]\n  (let [binding (when (frontend/ok? selected) (:binding selected))]\n    (when (and (map? binding) (fn? (:parse binding)) (fn? (:lower binding)))\n      binding)))\n\n\n(defn- frontend-binding\n  \"The installed binding for `lang` in the session's pinned catalog.  With\n   no parse and lower stage installed it throws an `unavailable-parser`\n   diagnostic: there is no fallback to another frontend.\"\n  [state lang]\n  (let [selected (select-frontend (:frontends state) lang)]\n    (or (usable-binding selected)\n        (throw (ex-info (str \"unavailable-parser: no parser for \" (pr-str lang))\n                        {:diagnostic :unavailable-parser\n                         :lang lang\n                         :selection selected})))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-parsed\n  \"Lower `parsed` through `binding`.  A binding with a `:lower-session`\n   stage lowers against the frontend session the shell keeps\n   (`:frontend-session`, cleared with the VM) and leaves the session it\n   answers, with the binding's `:render`, in the program's\n   `::frontend` metadata, for `eval-compiled` to stage.\"\n  [state binding parsed]\n  (let [lower-session (:lower-session binding)\n        [ast session] (if lower-session\n                        (lower-session parsed (:frontend-session state))\n                        [((:lower binding) parsed) nil])\n        staged (cond-> {}\n                 (:render binding) (assoc :render (:render binding))\n                 lower-session (assoc :session session)\n                 (:derive binding) (assoc :derivation ((:derive binding) parsed ast)))]\n    (cond-> ast\n      (seq staged) (vary-meta assoc ::frontend staged))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-input\n  \"Lower `input` through the selected frontend; `forms` are the shell\n   reader's forms, used by a frontend that consumes them.\"\n  [state input forms]\n  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n    (lower-parsed state binding\n                  ((:parse binding)\n                   (if (= :forms (:input binding)) forms input)))))\n\n\n(defn- forms-input?\n  [state]\n  (= :forms (:input (frontend-binding state (:lang state)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-source\n  [state input]\n  (let [binding (frontend-binding state (:lang state))]\n    (lower-parsed state binding\n                  ((:parse binding)\n                   (if (= :forms (:input binding)) (read-forms input) input)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-command-ast\n  \"The AST `(compile ...)` previews.  It lowers against a primed frontend\n   session: a session-staged frontend carries its prelude only on the\n   session's first lowering, and the preview is of the submitted form, not\n   of the runtime it would run on.  The session itself is not touched.\"\n  [state arg]\n  (let [state (assoc state :frontend-session :primed)]\n    (cond\n      (string? arg) (compile-source state arg)\n      (forms-input? state) (compile-input state nil [arg])\n      :else (throw (ex-info \"This compile command expects a source string\"\n                            {:lang (:lang state) :arg arg})))))\n\n\n(defn- render-compile-output","numLines":80,"startLine":2395,"totalLines":3025}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_1bcb507731e14720933179e8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
