{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126202536c77ccb5f29b04904","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. `clj/collection-key` refuses float keys via `data/admit-key?` → `:coll/unsupported-key` policy. That's the runtime key admission.\n\nNow let me look at the corpus test (clojure_collection_order_test.cljc) to understand its structure — the corpus mechanism, how the reference is recorded, and the r2 narrowed rows. This is central for gate 3.","signature":"819212bcfb8a4a34a1bb66aa"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"788e531f-5391-467e-9cdf-9836269d390c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:25:39.740Z","thinking_duration_ms":1780,"thinking_display":"updates"}
