{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_69942c203fc541a0b3a5f150","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\n2\t  \"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\n3\t   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\n4\t   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\n5\t   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\n6\t   c1-2 revision.\n7\t\n8\t   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\n9\t   emitter's own sort: children project through\n10\t   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\n11\t   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\n12\t   same comparator the ruling names -- never through the helper under test.\"\n13\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]])\n14\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n15\t            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n16\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n17\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n18\t            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\n19\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n20\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n21\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n22\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n23\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n24\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n25\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n26\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n27\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n28\t            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n29\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n30\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n31\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n32\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t;; =============================================================================\n36\t;; Independent oracle builders (RULING 1's comparator, not the emitter's sort)\n37\t;; =============================================================================\n38\t\n39\t(defn- collection-applications\n40\t  \"Every constructor application of compiled `ast` -- an assoc over the {}\n41\t   seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed -- in outermost-first walk order. A\n42\t   program under test contains either only emitter output or only the\n43\t   explicit constructor calls a control names, never both.\"\n44\t  [ast]\n45\t  (let [acc (atom [])]\n46\t    (walk/postwalk\n47\t      (fn [n]\n48\t        (when (and (map? n)\n49\t                   (= :application (:type n))\n50\t                   (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\n51\t                   (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\n52\t                   (contains? #{[(quote assoc) {}] [(quote conj) []] [(quote conj) #{}]}\n53\t                              [(get-in n [:operator :name])\n54\t                               (get-in n [:operands 0 :value])]))\n55\t          (swap! acc conj n))\n56\t        n)\n57\t      ast)\n58\t    @acc))\n59\t\n60\t\n61\t(defn- child-roots\n62\t  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of each operand of `node`,\n63\t   projected independently of the emitter.\"\n64\t  [node]\n65\t  (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) (:operands node)))\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn- map-constructors\n69\t  [ast]\n70\t  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\n71\t        (collection-applications ast)))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(def ^:private empty-map-seed-root\n75\t  \"The content address of the {} seed literal: host- and revision-stable.\"\n76\t  :segment/blake3-201f235cbac998f43954454e9df0eb633717e79de535776f3f51e198a3759b10)\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t(defn- pair-keys\n80\t  \"The RULING 1 sort keys of a map constructor's pairs: `[key-root\n81\t   value-root]` per source pair, in emitted order.\"\n82\t  [node]\n83\t  (mapv vec (partition 2 (rest (child-roots node)))))\n84\t\n85\t\n86\t(defn- element-keys\n87\t  \"The RULING 1 sort keys of a set constructor's elements (one root each),\n88\t   in emitted order.\"\n89\t  [node]\n90\t  (mapv vector (rest (child-roots node))))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(defn- strictly-ascending?\n94\t  \"True when `ks` sorts strictly ascending by jing/canonical-compare: every\n95\t   adjacent pair compares negative. The strict form deliberately does NOT\n96\t   certify a tie (equal adjacent keys are equal executable content and a\n97\t   legal emitted order, but not a strictly ascending one) -- blocks that\n98\t   construct a tie assert it directly or compare against the sequence's\n99\t   own non-descending sort instead.\"\n100\t  [ks]\n101\t  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\n102\t          (partition 2 1 ks)))\n103\t\n104\t\n105\t(defn- key-literals\n106\t  \"The literal values at the key positions of a map constructor (every\n107\t   second operand after the seed), for reading an emitted order.\"\n108\t  [node]\n109\t  (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (:value o)))\n110\t        (take-nth 2 (rest (:operands node)))))\n111\t\n112\t\n113\t(defn- project-batch\n114\t  \"One compiled ast through the production encoder envelope under `token`.\"\n115\t  ([ast] (project-batch ast \"order-a\"))\n116\t  ([ast token]\n117\t   (let [p (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n118\t     {:tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n119\t      :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)})))\n120\t\n121\t\n122\t(defn- digest-snapshot\n123\t  \"The equality snapshot of one projected batch: root, the canonical-sorted\n124\t   C1 marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector, and all three\n125\t   instruction formats' call-provenance -- the cohort's model, with nothing\n126\t   normalized away.\"\n127\t  [{:keys [tree rows]}]\n128\t  (let [c1 (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n129\t                      (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) rows)))\n130\t        keys (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n131\t                        (into [] (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n132\t                                       (map #(vec (take 3 %)))) rows)))\n133\t        sem (linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)\n134\t        stack (derive/stack-image (:vector sem)\n135\t                                  {:segment-address :order/stack\n136\t                                   :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\n137\t        register (derive/register-image (:vector sem)\n138\t                                        {:segment-address :order/register\n139\t                                         :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})]\n140\t    {:root (:root tree)\n141\t     :applications (count keys)\n142\t     :keys-digest (jing/content-hash keys)\n143\t     :c1-digest (jing/content-hash c1)\n144\t     :instruction-provenance-digest\n145\t     (jing/content-hash [(:call-provenance sem)\n146\t                         (:call-provenance stack)\n147\t                         (:call-provenance register)])}))\n148\t\n149\t\n150\t(defn- compile-snapshot\n151\t  \"Compile `form`, project it, digest it.\"\n152\t  [form]\n153\t  (digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form))))\n154\t\n155\t\n156\t;; =============================================================================\n157\t;; Execution routes (RULING 2/3: walker, semantic, stack, register)\n158\t;; =============================================================================\n159\t\n160\t(def ^:private registry\n161\t  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n162\t      module/register-cell-module\n163\t      data/register-data-module))\n164\t\n165\t\n166\t(def ^:private base-opts\n167\t  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n168\t   :capability-secret tu/secret\n169\t   :primitives vm/primitives\n170\t   :modules registry})\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n174\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n175\t\n176\t\n177\t(def ^:private lanes\n178\t  \"The four execution routes the behavior tests run.\"\n179\t  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n180\t\n181\t\n182\t(defn- run-lane\n183\t  \"Run compiled `ast` on one execution route.\"\n184\t  [lane ast env]\n185\t  ;; the walker/semantic machines take :env; the debruijn machines take\n186\t  ;; :free-env for free names -- both spell the same test-supplied bindings\n187\t  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env :free-env env)]\n188\t    (case lane\n189\t      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\n190\t      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n191\t                                           (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n192\t      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n193\t                       (:image (derive/stack-image\n194\t                                 (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\n195\t                       (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\n196\t      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n197\t                          (derive/register-image\n198\t                            (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n199\t                          (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"6e841fbe-e346-4e9b-b4f9-cd597ff5fddb","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:25:39.818Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc","content":"(ns yang.clojure-collection-order-test\n  \"Constructed collections v1 (architect ruling 1795017757000, RULING 1-4):\n   the canonical operand ordering of dynamically constructed map and set\n   literals at yang.clojure's collection emitter, the evaluation semantics\n   that ordering makes executable, and the manifest/legacy boundaries of the\n   c1-2 revision.\n\n   Every order expectation here comes from builders independent of the\n   emitter's own sort: children project through\n   yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode and order through dao.jing/canonical-compare\n   (RFC 8949 canonical bytes, unsigned bytewise, proper prefix first), the\n   same comparator the ruling names -- never through the helper under test.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]])\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.stream.base64 :as base64]\n            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Independent oracle builders (RULING 1's comparator, not the emitter's sort)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- collection-applications\n  \"Every constructor application of compiled `ast` -- an assoc over the {}\n   seed or a conj over the []/#{} seed -- in outermost-first walk order. A\n   program under test contains either only emitter output or only the\n   explicit constructor calls a control names, never both.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [acc (atom [])]\n    (walk/postwalk\n      (fn [n]\n        (when (and (map? n)\n                   (= :application (:type n))\n                   (= :variable (get-in n [:operator :type]))\n                   (= :literal (get-in n [:operands 0 :type]))\n                   (contains? #{[(quote assoc) {}] [(quote conj) []] [(quote conj) #{}]}\n                              [(get-in n [:operator :name])\n                               (get-in n [:operands 0 :value])]))\n          (swap! acc conj n))\n        n)\n      ast)\n    @acc))\n\n\n(defn- child-roots\n  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of each operand of `node`,\n   projected independently of the emitter.\"\n  [node]\n  (mapv (fn [o] (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode o))) (:operands node)))\n\n\n(defn- map-constructors\n  [ast]\n  (into [] (filter #(= (quote assoc) (get-in % [:operator :name])))\n        (collection-applications ast)))\n\n\n(def ^:private empty-map-seed-root\n  \"The content address of the {} seed literal: host- and revision-stable.\"\n  :segment/blake3-201f235cbac998f43954454e9df0eb633717e79de535776f3f51e198a3759b10)\n\n\n(defn- pair-keys\n  \"The RULING 1 sort keys of a map constructor's pairs: `[key-root\n   value-root]` per source pair, in emitted order.\"\n  [node]\n  (mapv vec (partition 2 (rest (child-roots node)))))\n\n\n(defn- element-keys\n  \"The RULING 1 sort keys of a set constructor's elements (one root each),\n   in emitted order.\"\n  [node]\n  (mapv vector (rest (child-roots node))))\n\n\n(defn- strictly-ascending?\n  \"True when `ks` sorts strictly ascending by jing/canonical-compare: every\n   adjacent pair compares negative. The strict form deliberately does NOT\n   certify a tie (equal adjacent keys are equal executable content and a\n   legal emitted order, but not a strictly ascending one) -- blocks that\n   construct a tie assert it directly or compare against the sequence's\n   own non-descending sort instead.\"\n  [ks]\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\n          (partition 2 1 ks)))\n\n\n(defn- key-literals\n  \"The literal values at the key positions of a map constructor (every\n   second operand after the seed), for reading an emitted order.\"\n  [node]\n  (mapv (fn [o] (when (= :literal (:type o)) (:value o)))\n        (take-nth 2 (rest (:operands node)))))\n\n\n(defn- project-batch\n  \"One compiled ast through the production encoder envelope under `token`.\"\n  ([ast] (project-batch ast \"order-a\"))\n  ([ast token]\n   (let [p (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n     {:tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n      :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)})))\n\n\n(defn- digest-snapshot\n  \"The equality snapshot of one projected batch: root, the canonical-sorted\n   C1 marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector, and all three\n   instruction formats' call-provenance -- the cohort's model, with nothing\n   normalized away.\"\n  [{:keys [tree rows]}]\n  (let [c1 (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n                      (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)) rows)))\n        keys (vec (sort jing/canonical-compare\n                        (into [] (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n                                       (map #(vec (take 3 %)))) rows)))\n        sem (linearize/project-rows tree nil rows)\n        stack (derive/stack-image (:vector sem)\n                                  {:segment-address :order/stack\n                                   :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})\n        register (derive/register-image (:vector sem)\n                                        {:segment-address :order/register\n                                         :call-provenance (:call-provenance sem)})]\n    {:root (:root tree)\n     :applications (count keys)\n     :keys-digest (jing/content-hash keys)\n     :c1-digest (jing/content-hash c1)\n     :instruction-provenance-digest\n     (jing/content-hash [(:call-provenance sem)\n                         (:call-provenance stack)\n                         (:call-provenance register)])}))\n\n\n(defn- compile-snapshot\n  \"Compile `form`, project it, digest it.\"\n  [form]\n  (digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Execution routes (RULING 2/3: walker, semantic, stack, register)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private registry\n  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n      module/register-cell-module\n      data/register-data-module))\n\n\n(def ^:private base-opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\n   :primitives vm/primitives\n   :modules registry})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(def ^:private lanes\n  \"The four execution routes the behavior tests run.\"\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- run-lane\n  \"Run compiled `ast` on one execution route.\"\n  [lane ast env]\n  ;; the walker/semantic machines take :env; the debruijn machines take\n  ;; :free-env for free names -- both spell the same test-supplied bindings\n  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :env env :free-env env)]\n    (case lane\n      :ast-walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)\n      :semantic (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                           (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n      :stack (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                       (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                 (:vector (linearize/project ast))))\n                       (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))\n      :register (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n                          (derive/register-image\n                            (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n                          (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))))\n","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1592}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_69942c203fc541a0b3a5f150","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
