{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_fdb54980c6bf447981010d54","type":"tool_result","content":"2930\t\n2931\t(defn- input-probe\n2932\t  \"The completeness probe of the session's frontend, or nil when it has\n2933\t   none or none is installed (the compile then reports it).\"\n2934\t  [state]\n2935\t  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n2936\t\n2937\t\n2938\t(defn eval-input\n2939\t  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n2940\t\n2941\t   Input that is not yet a whole submission is retained as `:pending-input`\n2942\t   and produces no text: for a frontend with a `:probe` the probe decides\n2943\t   and the line is kept verbatim (whitespace can be inside a string);\n2944\t   otherwise the brackets must balance. The endpoint passes a refusal for\n2945\t   store changes so the same reader and command dispatch enforce isolation.\"\n2946\t  ([state line] (eval-input state line nil))\n2947\t  ([state line store-command-refusal]\n2948\t   (let [probe (input-probe state)\n2949\t         pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n2950\t         line (if probe line (str/trim line))\n2951\t         combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n2952\t                    line\n2953\t                    (str pending \"\\n\" line))]\n2954\t     (cond\n2955\t       (and probe (str/blank? combined))\n2956\t       [(assoc state :pending-input nil) \"\"]\n2957\t\n2958\t       (if probe\n2959\t         (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n2960\t         (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n2961\t       [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n2962\t\n2963\t       :else\n2964\t       (let [parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n2965\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n2966\t                                   :clj Exception\n2967\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n2968\t                           {:error error}))]\n2969\t         (if (and store-command-refusal (command-line? parsed)\n2970\t                  (= 'use-store (ffirst (:forms parsed))))\n2971\t           [(assoc state :pending-input nil) store-command-refusal]\n2972\t           (eval-parsed (assoc state :pending-input nil) combined parsed)))))))\n2973\t\n2974\t\n2975\t(defn repl-state\n2976\t  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n2977\t\n2978\t   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n2979\t   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n2980\t   operation.\n2981\t   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n2982\t   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n2983\t   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n2984\t   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n2985\t   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n2986\t   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n2987\t   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n2988\t   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n2989\t   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n2990\t   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n2991\t   `:index-publication` exposes the verified code-log cursor and covered\n2992\t   transaction count for owner diagnostics, never a substitute query view.\n2993\t   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n2994\t   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n2995\t   failed.\"\n2996\t  [state]\n2997\t  {:lang (:lang state)\n2998\t   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n2999\t                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n3000\t                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n3001\t                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n3002\t   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n3003\t        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n3004\t        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n3005\t        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n3006\t                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n3007\t                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n3008\t   :running? (:running? state)\n3009\t   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n3010\t            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n3011\t   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n3012\t              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n3013\t                (mapv (fn [p]\n3014\t                        {:name (:name p)\n3015\t                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n3016\t                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n3017\t                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n3018\t                      (:links parked))))\n3019\t   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n3020\t   :index-publication (select-keys (get-in state [:indexer :materialization])\n3021\t                                   [:cursor :transactions])\n3022\t   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n3023\t   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n3024\t   :remote {:connected? false}})\n3025\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"ee0d2e2e-34dc-4937-aef1-488569432030","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:26:11.848Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc","content":"\n(defn- input-probe\n  \"The completeness probe of the session's frontend, or nil when it has\n   none or none is installed (the compile then reports it).\"\n  [state]\n  (:probe (usable-binding (select-frontend (:frontends state) (:lang state)))))\n\n\n(defn eval-input\n  \"Evaluate one input line locally, returning `[state text]`.\n\n   Input that is not yet a whole submission is retained as `:pending-input`\n   and produces no text: for a frontend with a `:probe` the probe decides\n   and the line is kept verbatim (whitespace can be inside a string);\n   otherwise the brackets must balance. The endpoint passes a refusal for\n   store changes so the same reader and command dispatch enforce isolation.\"\n  ([state line] (eval-input state line nil))\n  ([state line store-command-refusal]\n   (let [probe (input-probe state)\n         pending (or (:pending-input state) \"\")\n         line (if probe line (str/trim line))\n         combined (if (str/blank? pending)\n                    line\n                    (str pending \"\\n\" line))]\n     (cond\n       (and probe (str/blank? combined))\n       [(assoc state :pending-input nil) \"\"]\n\n       (if probe\n         (= :incomplete (probe combined))\n         (pos? (bracket-balance combined)))\n       [(assoc state :pending-input combined) \"\"]\n\n       :else\n       (let [parsed (try {:forms (read-forms combined)}\n                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                   :clj Exception\n                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n                           {:error error}))]\n         (if (and store-command-refusal (command-line? parsed)\n                  (= 'use-store (ffirst (:forms parsed))))\n           [(assoc state :pending-input nil) store-command-refusal]\n           (eval-parsed (assoc state :pending-input nil) combined parsed)))))))\n\n\n(defn repl-state\n  \"A serializable summary of shell state.\n\n   The stream summaries read the ledger rather than asking a handle whether it\n   is closed: dao.stream has no `closed?`, and an idle medium has no last\n   operation.\n   The program media are the composition's own, observed beside the VM, so\n   the shell reports what it knows of them — the declared capacity, the gaps\n   the session's observers counted, and whether a loss has already refused\n   further evaluation.  Each `:pending` entry carries the link policy's\n   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n   can display why a run is still waiting (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   section 3.5).  `:macros` maps each macro the expander's store holds\n   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n   `:index-publication` exposes the verified code-log cursor and covered\n   transaction count for owner diagnostics, never a substitute query view.\n   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n   of its `$ast` and `$occ` relations, whether a gap lost it, and why it\n   failed.\"\n  [state]\n  {:lang (:lang state)\n   :macros (into (sorted-map-by #(compare (str %1) (str %2)))\n                 (map (fn [[sym entry]]\n                        [sym (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))]))\n                 (get-in state [:expander :ctx :store]))\n   :vm {:type (:vm-type state)\n        :halted? (vm/halted? (:vm state))\n        :blocked? (vm/blocked? (:vm state))\n        :in-stream {:capacity ingress-capacity\n                    :gaps (ingress-gaps state)\n                    :lost? (boolean (:ingress-loss? state))}}\n   :running? (:running? state)\n   :output {:cursor (:output-cursor state)\n            :last-outcome (get-in state [:ledger :output] :untried)}\n   :pending (when-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n              (let [policy (:link-policy state)]\n                (mapv (fn [p]\n                        {:name (:name p)\n                         :link-id (:yin.link/id p)\n                         :policy (if (fn? policy) :fn policy)\n                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n                      (:links parked))))\n   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n   :index-publication (select-keys (get-in state [:indexer :materialization])\n                                   [:cursor :transactions])\n   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n   :telemetry {:supported? false :note telemetry-text}\n   :remote {:connected? false}})\n","numLines":96,"startLine":2930,"totalLines":3025}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_fdb54980c6bf447981010d54","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
