{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126202703604b7ce6b9964f4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The three demos read source with `cljs.reader/read-string` then compile forms (via yang.clojure/compile presumably). These are browser demos (cljs only). After my fix, the honest migration is to route them through `yang.clojure/read-forms` (the frontend source entry) instead of cljs.reader — that's a one-line change per demo, and they are in the audit list (\"migrate actual compilation callers or explicitly delimit their legacy raw-forms behavior\"). They're .cljs files — yang.clojure/read-forms works on :cljs. I'll migrate them (they compile source strings, so this is exactly the migration the ruling wants).\n\nLet me look at what they do after reading — equation_plotter:271.","signature":"a18432b8278848e29cd33fcf"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"1c6c3300-916b-4e64-af99-52cbd17ca5b5","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:27:07.177Z","thinking_duration_ms":2779,"thinking_display":"updates"}
