{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_c2b4978557a7458e826ad4af","type":"tool_result","content":"790\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n791\t                   ring/capacity-key output-capacity})))\n792\t\n793\t\n794\t(defn- mint-cursor\n795\t  [handle]\n796\t  (let [result (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest)]\n797\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n798\t      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n799\t\n800\t\n801\t;; =============================================================================\n802\t;; The VM and its program medium\n803\t;; =============================================================================\n804\t\n805\t(defn- make-ring-stream\n806\t  \"The `:make-stream` the shell hands the VM: one ring buffer per call.  A\n807\t   nil capacity is the VM's default, not an unbounded stream; dao.stream has\n808\t   no unbounded mode.\"\n809\t  [capacity]\n810\t  (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n811\t                 ring/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n812\t\n813\t\n814\t(defn make-vm\n815\t  \"Construct the shell's evaluator on `yin.vm`.\n816\t\n817\t   The shell is the composition that chooses the VM's transport: the\n818\t   evaluator is handed `:make-stream` bound to the ring buffer and the\n819\t   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\n820\t   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\n821\t   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\n822\t\n823\t   `extra-primitives` is the host-supplied map merged over the REPL's own\n824\t   primitives, so an embedding host's functions win a name collision.\n825\t\n826\t   `link-pair` is the link pair `(require ...)` lowers to\n827\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 6.1), held in the VM's private `:resources`\n828\t   table; `make-session` composes one per VM, and the install children\n829\t   the VM starts inherit it.\n830\t\n831\t   `query-pair` is the session's query call pair\n832\t   (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`), supplied as the VM's FFI pair with its\n833\t   call-out cursor; with it the registry carries the query bridge, so\n834\t   `(require 'dao.space.query)` activates `dao.space.query/q`.\n835\t\n836\t   `host-modules` is the composition's own module registrations,\n837\t   `{module-name (fn [registry] registry')}`: the generic mechanism a\n838\t   composition registers the host modules it serves through\n839\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 6).  This namespace\n840\t   registers none of its own beyond the query bridge, and never names a\n841\t   module it does not serve.\"\n842\t  ([vm-type output-stream] (make-vm vm-type output-stream nil nil nil nil))\n843\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n844\t   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives nil nil nil))\n845\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair]\n846\t   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair nil nil))\n847\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair]\n848\t   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair nil))\n849\t  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair host-modules]\n850\t   (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n851\t     (throw (ex-info \"Unknown Yin REPL VM type\"\n852\t                     {:vm-type vm-type\n853\t                      :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n854\t   ((get vm-constructors vm-type)\n855\t    (cond-> {:primitives (merge (make-repl-primitives output-stream)\n856\t                                extra-primitives)\n857\t             :modules (cond-> (-> (module/default-registry)\n858\t                                  module/register-stream-module\n859\t                                  module/register-cell-module\n860\t                                  (data/register-data-module\n861\t                                    {::data/max-items 1048576})\n862\t                                  (integer/register-integer-module\n863\t                                    {::integer/max-bits 100000\n864\t                                     ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n865\t                                  php-prelude/admit)\n866\t                        query-pair (query/register host-modules))\n867\t             :make-stream make-ring-stream\n868\t             ;; the task's capability secret (yin.vm.linker.md 7.3, r10):\n869\t             ;; the REPL is the composition, so it mints one from its own\n870\t             ;; random source, and a fresh one for every install child the\n871\t             ;; task starts\n872\t             :capability-secret (str (random-uuid))\n873\t             :secret-source (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid)))}\n874\t      link-pair (assoc :link-request (:requests link-pair)\n875\t                       :link-response (:responses link-pair))\n876\t      query-pair (assoc :call-in (:call-in query-pair)\n877\t                        :call-out (:call-out query-pair)\n878\t                        :call-out-cursor (:out-cursor query-pair))))))\n879\t\n880\t\n881\t(defn- make-runner\n882\t  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\n883\t   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\n884\t   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\n885\t   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\n886\t   from that stream, never from the VM record; the append outcome rides\n887\t   back on the VM as `::result-append`, so a refused append is reported\n888\t   rather than silently lost.\"\n889\t  [output-stream round]\n890\t  (fn [vm]\n891\t    (let [vm' (vm/run vm)]\n892\t      (if (vm/halted? vm')\n893\t        (assoc vm'\n894\t               ::result-append\n895\t               (emit-result! output-stream round (vm/value vm')))\n896\t        vm'))))\n897\t\n898\t\n899\t(defn- make-attachment\n900\t  \"Create one composition-owned medium of `capacity` elements, the unary\n901\t   attachment entry bound to it for this medium's lifetime, and an observer\n902\t   attached through that entry.  `:attach` attaches a further, independently\n903\t   advanced observer through the same entry.\n904\t\n905\t   The resolver maps the descriptor's identity to the owner handle this\n906\t   composition created, which is host composition around the ring buffer's own\n907\t   attach mechanism: the observer itself sees only a descriptor and a unary\n908\t   capability, so no transport detail crosses into it.\"\n909\t  [capacity]\n910\t  (let [writer (:dao.stream/handle\n911\t                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n912\t                                ring/capacity-key capacity}))\n913\t        described (stream/descriptor writer)\n914\t        descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor described)\n915\t        identity (:dao.stream/identity described)\n916\t        attach! (ring/make-attacher {(:dao.stream/identity descriptor) writer})]\n917\t    {:stream writer\n918\t     :identity identity\n919\t     :observer (observer/attach attach! descriptor)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"c0169331-9506-4e82-8272-836cf411553d","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:28:10.622Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc","content":"    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                   ring/capacity-key output-capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- mint-cursor\n  [handle]\n  (let [result (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest)]\n    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The VM and its program medium\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- make-ring-stream\n  \"The `:make-stream` the shell hands the VM: one ring buffer per call.  A\n   nil capacity is the VM's default, not an unbounded stream; dao.stream has\n   no unbounded mode.\"\n  [capacity]\n  (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                 ring/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n\n\n(defn make-vm\n  \"Construct the shell's evaluator on `yin.vm`.\n\n   The shell is the composition that chooses the VM's transport: the\n   evaluator is handed `:make-stream` bound to the ring buffer and the\n   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\n   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\n   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\n\n   `extra-primitives` is the host-supplied map merged over the REPL's own\n   primitives, so an embedding host's functions win a name collision.\n\n   `link-pair` is the link pair `(require ...)` lowers to\n   (yin.vm.linker.md section 6.1), held in the VM's private `:resources`\n   table; `make-session` composes one per VM, and the install children\n   the VM starts inherit it.\n\n   `query-pair` is the session's query call pair\n   (`yin.repl.query/make-pair`), supplied as the VM's FFI pair with its\n   call-out cursor; with it the registry carries the query bridge, so\n   `(require 'dao.space.query)` activates `dao.space.query/q`.\n\n   `host-modules` is the composition's own module registrations,\n   `{module-name (fn [registry] registry')}`: the generic mechanism a\n   composition registers the host modules it serves through\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 6).  This namespace\n   registers none of its own beyond the query bridge, and never names a\n   module it does not serve.\"\n  ([vm-type output-stream] (make-vm vm-type output-stream nil nil nil nil))\n  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives]\n   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives nil nil nil))\n  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair]\n   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair nil nil))\n  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair]\n   (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair nil))\n  ([vm-type output-stream extra-primitives link-pair query-pair host-modules]\n   (when-not (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n     (throw (ex-info \"Unknown Yin REPL VM type\"\n                     {:vm-type vm-type\n                      :supported (vec (keys vm-constructors))})))\n   ((get vm-constructors vm-type)\n    (cond-> {:primitives (merge (make-repl-primitives output-stream)\n                                extra-primitives)\n             :modules (cond-> (-> (module/default-registry)\n                                  module/register-stream-module\n                                  module/register-cell-module\n                                  (data/register-data-module\n                                    {::data/max-items 1048576})\n                                  (integer/register-integer-module\n                                    {::integer/max-bits 100000\n                                     ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n                                  php-prelude/admit)\n                        query-pair (query/register host-modules))\n             :make-stream make-ring-stream\n             ;; the task's capability secret (yin.vm.linker.md 7.3, r10):\n             ;; the REPL is the composition, so it mints one from its own\n             ;; random source, and a fresh one for every install child the\n             ;; task starts\n             :capability-secret (str (random-uuid))\n             :secret-source (fn [_origin] (str (random-uuid)))}\n      link-pair (assoc :link-request (:requests link-pair)\n                       :link-response (:responses link-pair))\n      query-pair (assoc :call-in (:call-in query-pair)\n                        :call-out (:call-out query-pair)\n                        :call-out-cursor (:out-cursor query-pair))))))\n\n\n(defn- make-runner\n  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\n   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\n   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\n   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\n   from that stream, never from the VM record; the append outcome rides\n   back on the VM as `::result-append`, so a refused append is reported\n   rather than silently lost.\"\n  [output-stream round]\n  (fn [vm]\n    (let [vm' (vm/run vm)]\n      (if (vm/halted? vm')\n        (assoc vm'\n               ::result-append\n               (emit-result! output-stream round (vm/value vm')))\n        vm'))))\n\n\n(defn- make-attachment\n  \"Create one composition-owned medium of `capacity` elements, the unary\n   attachment entry bound to it for this medium's lifetime, and an observer\n   attached through that entry.  `:attach` attaches a further, independently\n   advanced observer through the same entry.\n\n   The resolver maps the descriptor's identity to the owner handle this\n   composition created, which is host composition around the ring buffer's own\n   attach mechanism: the observer itself sees only a descriptor and a unary\n   capability, so no transport detail crosses into it.\"\n  [capacity]\n  (let [writer (:dao.stream/handle\n                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n                                ring/capacity-key capacity}))\n        described (stream/descriptor writer)\n        descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor described)\n        identity (:dao.stream/identity described)\n        attach! (ring/make-attacher {(:dao.stream/identity descriptor) writer})]\n    {:stream writer\n     :identity identity\n     :observer (observer/attach attach! descriptor)","numLines":130,"startLine":790,"totalLines":3025}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_c2b497855