{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_39ab95cea7d64008b709954d","type":"tool_result","content":"525\t        :else (compare (pr-str a) (pr-str b))))\n526\t\n527\t\n528\t(defn- typed-map\n529\t  \"A `:type`-tagged value — `{:type :closure ...}`, `{:type :host-fn ...}` —\n530\t   prints `:type` first, then its other keys in printed order. Map\n531\t   iteration order is host-dependent (ClojureDart's small maps don't keep\n532\t   insertion order), so a fixed order is what makes the rendered text the\n533\t   same on every host.\"\n534\t  [entries]\n535\t  (into (sorted-map-by typed-key-compare) entries))\n536\t\n537\t\n538\t(defn- host-fn-marker\n539\t  \"A host function renders as `{:type :host-fn :name '<name>}`, shaped like\n540\t   a data closure's `{:type :closure ...}` so the two read side by side and\n541\t   `:type` tells them apart. The host object itself never prints: its form\n542\t   differs per host and leaks class names and addresses.\"\n543\t  [namer f]\n544\t  (let [n (when namer (namer f))]\n545\t    (typed-map (cond-> [[:type :host-fn]] n (conj [:name (list 'quote n)])))))\n546\t\n547\t\n548\t(defn- rendered-text\n549\t  [x]\n550\t  (str/trimr (pretty/pp-str x)))\n551\t\n552\t\n553\t(deftype DisplayKey\n554\t  [text rank]\n555\t  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/IPrint (-print [_ sink] (.write sink text))]\n556\t      :cljs [IPrintWithWriter (-pr-writer [_ writer _opts] (-write writer text))]))\n557\t\n558\t\n559\t#?(:cljd nil\n560\t   :clj (defmethod print-method DisplayKey\n561\t          [k ^java.io.Writer w]\n562\t          (.write w ^String (.-text ^DisplayKey k))))\n563\t\n564\t\n565\t(defn- display-order\n566\t  [[type-a key-a value-a] [type-b key-b value-b]]\n567\t  (let [c (compare type-a type-b)]\n568\t    (if-not (zero? c)\n569\t      c\n570\t      (let [c (compare key-a key-b)]\n571\t        (if (zero? c) (compare value-a value-b) c)))))\n572\t\n573\t\n574\t(defn- display-map\n575\t  \"Rendering can make distinct key