then (M)? — \"1M\" → m1=\"1\", m4=\"M\" → BigDecimal 1. So \"1M\" is a BigDecimal via float-pattern! And tools.reader match... on JVM tools.reader: read \"1M\" → BigDecimal ONE. On JS match-float with M → parseFloat(\"1\") → 1 Number (INTEGER content!). Confirmed relabel bug for \"1M\" on JS.\n\nJS carriers: dao.host.number/->Rational (exported via cbor/->Rational!) and Decimal — how to construct Decimal on JS? Check number.cljc lines 148-170 (deftype Decimal ...). Constructor (Decimal. ...) — exported from dao.host.number as...? cbor/decimal? checks. Let me look at the Decimal deftype + any parse helper.","signature":"a0b3964a1ce34b10971603b9"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"80e18efb-5298-4755-9980-9305ce1b52a4","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:38:51.568Z","thinking_duration_ms":13019,"thinking_display":"updates"}
