{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_ea1e93db1be142e3959ced8f","type":"tool_result","content":"218\t\n219\t\n220\t(defn decimal?\n221\t  \"P. True for decimal content: `BigDecimal` on the JVM, the `Decimal`\n222\t   carrier on JS and Dart.\"\n223\t  [x]\n224\t  #?(:cljd (instance? Decimal x)\n225\t     :clj (instance? BigDecimal x)\n226\t     :cljs (instance? Decimal x)))\n227\t\n228\t\n229\t(def decimal-exponent-min\n230\t  \"Smallest decimal exponent every host accepts: the JVM scale\n231\t   (-exponent) is a 32-bit int, so -(2^31 - 1).\"\n232\t  -2147483647)\n233\t\n234\t\n235\t(def decimal-exponent-max\n236\t  \"Largest decimal exponent every host accepts: 2^31 (scale -2^31).\"\n237\t  2147483648)\n238\t\n239\t\n240\t(defn decimal-of\n241\t  \"P, fresh. Decimal content `mantissa x 10^exponent` with exactly this\n242\t   scale, for exact integers `exponent` and `mantissa`. Every host accepts\n243\t   exactly the exponents in [decimal-exponent-min, decimal-exponent-max],\n244\t   the JVM `BigDecimal` window, so acceptance never depends on the host;\n245\t   outside it the value is refused `:malformed-number`.\"\n246\t  [exponent mantissa]\n247\t  (let [e (big 'decimal-of exponent)\n248\t        m (big 'decimal-of mantissa)]\n249\t    (when-not (and (<= 0 (integer/compare-big e (integer/promote decimal-exponent-min)))\n250\t                   (<= (integer/compare-big e (integer/promote decimal-exponent-max)) 0))\n251\t      (refuse 'decimal-of :malformed-number \"decimal exponent out of range\"))\n252\t    #?(:cljd (Decimal. (.toInt ^BigInt e) m)\n253\t       :clj (BigDecimal. ^BigInteger m (int (- (.longValue ^BigInteger e))))\n254\t       :cljs (Decimal. (js/Number e) m))))\n255\t\n256\t\n257\t(defn decimal-exponent\n258\t  \"P. The exponent of decimal content `d`, a native integer.\"\n259\t  [d]\n260\t  #?(:cljd (.-exponent ^Decimal d)\n261\t     :clj (- (.scale ^BigDecimal d))\n262\t     :cljs (.-exponent ^Decimal d)))\n263\t\n264\t\n265\t(defn decimal-mantissa\n266\t  \"P. The exact mantissa of decimal content `d` as a host big integer.\"\n267\t  [d]\n268\t  #?(:cljd (.-mantissa ^Decimal d)\n269\t     :clj (.unscaledValue ^BigDecimal d)\n270\t     :cljs (.-mantissa ^Decimal d)))\n271\t\n272\t\n273\t(defn ratio?\n274\t  \"P. True for rational content: `clojure.lang.Ratio` or the `Rational`\n275\t   carrier.\"\n276\t  [x]\n277\t  #?(:cljd (instance? Rational x)\n278\t     :clj (or (instance? clojure.lang.Ratio x) (instance? Rational x))\n279\t     :cljs (instance? Rational x)))\n280\t\n281\t\n282\t(defn ratio-of\n283\t  \"P, fresh. Rational content `numerator/denominator` for exact integers,\n284\t   reduced, with the sign on the numerator; both fields are host big\n285\t   integers. Denominator 1 keeps rational kind (a `Rational` carrier); on\n286\t   the JVM other ratios are `clojure.lang.Ratio`. A zero denominator is\n287\t   refused `:malformed-number`.\"\n288\t  [numerator denominator]\n289\t  (let [n (big 'ratio-of numerator)\n290\t        d (big 'ratio-of denominator)]\n291\t    (when (zero? (integer/compare-big d zero))\n292\t      (refuse 'ratio-of :malformed-number \"zero denominator\"))\n293\t    (let [[n d] (if (neg? (integer/compare-big d zero))\n294\t                  [(integer/sub zero n) (integer/sub zero d)]\n295\t                  [n d])\n296\t          g (integer/gcd n d)\n297\t          n (integer/quot-trunc n g)\n298\t          d (integer/quot-trunc d g)]\n299\t      #?(:cljd (Rational. n d)\n300\t         :clj (if (= (integer/from-native 1) d)\n301\t                (Rational. n d)\n302\t                (clojure.lang.Ratio. ^BigInteger n ^BigInteger d))\n303\t         :cljs (Rational. n d)))))\n304\t\n305\t\n306\t(defn ratio-numerator\n307\t  \"P. The numerator of rational content `r`, a host big integer.\"\n308\t  [r]\n309\t  #?(:cljd (.-numerator ^Rational r)\n310\t     :clj (if (instance? Rational r)\n311\t            (.-numerator ^Rational r)\n312\t            (.numerator ^clojure.lang.Ratio r))\n313\t     :cljs (.-numerator ^Rational r)))\n314\t\n315\t\n316\t(defn ratio-denominator\n317\t  \"P. The denominator of rational content `r`, a positive host big\n318\t   integer.\"\n319\t  [r]\n320\t  #?(:cljd (.-denominator ^Rational r)\n321\t     :clj (if (instance? Rational r)\n322\t            (.-denominator ^Rational r)\n323\t            (.denominator ^clojure.lang.Ratio r))\n324\t     :cljs (.-denominator ^Rational r)))\n325\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"2e971985-2d10-4296-af48-985976faea04","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:39:04.536Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc","content":"\n\n(defn decimal?\n  \"P. True for decimal content: `BigDecimal` on the JVM, the `Decimal`\n   carrier on JS and Dart.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (instance? Decimal x)\n     :clj (instance? BigDecimal x)\n     :cljs (instance? Decimal x)))\n\n\n(def decimal-exponent-min\n  \"Smallest decimal exponent every host accepts: the JVM scale\n   (-exponent) is a 32-bit int, so -(2^31 - 1).\"\n  -2147483647)\n\n\n(def decimal-exponent-max\n  \"Largest decimal exponent every host accepts: 2^31 (scale -2^31).\"\n  2147483648)\n\n\n(defn decimal-of\n  \"P, fresh. Decimal content `mantissa x 10^exponent` with exactly this\n   scale, for exact integers `exponent` and `mantissa`. Every host accepts\n   exactly the exponents in [decimal-exponent-min, decimal-exponent-max],\n   the JVM `BigDecimal` window, so acceptance never depends on the host;\n   outside it the value is refused `:malformed-number`.\"\n  [exponent mantissa]\n  (let [e (big 'decimal-of exponent)\n        m (big 'decimal-of mantissa)]\n    (when-not (and (<= 0 (integer/compare-big e (integer/promote decimal-exponent-min)))\n                   (<= (integer/compare-big e (integer/promote decimal-exponent-max)) 0))\n      (refuse 'decimal-of :malformed-number \"decimal exponent out of range\"))\n    #?(:cljd (Decimal. (.toInt ^BigInt e) m)\n       :clj (BigDecimal. ^BigInteger m (int (- (.longValue ^BigInteger e))))\n       :cljs (Decimal. (js/Number e) m))))\n\n\n(defn decimal-exponent\n  \"P. The exponent of decimal content `d`, a native integer.\"\n  [d]\n  #?(:cljd (.-exponent ^Decimal d)\n     :clj (- (.scale ^BigDecimal d))\n     :cljs (.-exponent ^Decimal d)))\n\n\n(defn decimal-mantissa\n  \"P. The exact mantissa of decimal content `d` as a host big integer.\"\n  [d]\n  #?(:cljd (.-mantissa ^Decimal d)\n     :clj (.unscaledValue ^BigDecimal d)\n     :cljs (.-mantissa ^Decimal d)))\n\n\n(defn ratio?\n  \"P. True for rational content: `clojure.lang.Ratio` or the `Rational`\n   carrier.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (instance? Rational x)\n     :clj (or (instance? clojure.lang.Ratio x) (instance? Rational x))\n     :cljs (instance? Rational x)))\n\n\n(defn ratio-of\n  \"P, fresh. Rational content `numerator/denominator` for exact integers,\n   reduced, with the sign on the numerator; both fields are host big\n   integers. Denominator 1 keeps rational kind (a `Rational` carrier); on\n   the JVM other ratios are `clojure.lang.Ratio`. A zero denominator is\n   refused `:malformed-number`.\"\n  [numerator denominator]\n  (let [n (big 'ratio-of numerator)\n        d (big 'ratio-of denominator)]\n    (when (zero? (integer/compare-big d zero))\n      (refuse 'ratio-of :malformed-number \"zero denominator\"))\n    (let [[n d] (if (neg? (integer/compare-big d zero))\n                  [(integer/sub zero n) (integer/sub zero d)]\n                  [n d])\n          g (integer/gcd n d)\n          n (integer/quot-trunc n g)\n          d (integer/quot-trunc d g)]\n      #?(:cljd (Rational. n d)\n         :clj (if (= (integer/from-native 1) d)\n                (Rational. n d)\n                (clojure.lang.Ratio. ^BigInteger n ^BigInteger d))\n         :cljs (Rational. n d)))))\n\n\n(defn ratio-numerator\n  \"P. The numerator of rational content `r`, a host big integer.\"\n  [r]\n  #?(:cljd (.-numerator ^Rational r)\n     :clj (if (instance? Rational r)\n            (.-numerator ^Rational r)\n            (.numerator ^clojure.lang.Ratio r))\n     :cljs (.-numerator ^Rational r)))\n\n\n(defn ratio-denominator\n  \"P. The denominator of rational content `r`, a positive host big\n   integer.\"\n  [r]\n  #?(:cljd (.-denominator ^Rational r)\n     :clj (if (instance? Rational r)\n            (.-denominator ^Rational r)\n            (.denominator ^clojure.lang.Ratio r))\n     :cljs (.-denominator ^Rational r)))\n","numLines":108,"startLine":218,"totalLines":325}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_ea1e93db1be142e3959ced8f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
