{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126204000215c7a0711cf44c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"IMPORTANT: `(compile (unless false 1 2))` — the compile command with a NON-STRING arg (a macro form!). Currently: forms-input → compile-input with [arg] → the macro form compiles/preview-expands. After my source-mode change, compile-command-ast would throw \"expects a source string\". This test would BREAK.\n\nLook at compile-command-ast again:\n\n```cljc\n(defn- compile-command-ast\n  [state arg]\n  (let [state (assoc state :frontend-session :primed)]\n    (cond\n      (string? arg) (compile-source state arg)\n      (forms-input? state) (compile-input state nil [arg])\n      :else (throw ...))))\n```\n\nOptions: keep a forms path for non-string args even in source mode — i.e. change the `:else` to `(compile-input state nil [arg])`? But compile-input with a source-mode binding passes the INPUT (the form object) to :parse — our reader expects a string. Hmm: `compile-input state nil [arg]` → `((:parse binding) (if (= :forms (:input binding)) forms input))` — input=nil! Broken.\n\nFix: in compile-command-ast, for non-string args when NOT forms-input, we should... The honest architecture: the preview command accepts a source STRING. `(compile (unless false 1 2))` — the shell READ the form (kind lost for floats, but for macro preview the arg is structure). The macro expansion happens in the preview lowering. If we route the form through our source reader we'd need source text — the shell has it (the raw line)! handle-command receives `args` (read forms), not the raw text. Hmm.\n\nOption: keep the Clojure binding as `:input :forms` BUT make the SHELL pass source... no — the shell's forms come from its own lossy reader.\n\nOption: for the Clojure frontend keep a SEPARATE forms-consuming entry for the preview command: `compile-command-ast` calls `clojure-lower`-equivalent on the read form directly: `((:lower