{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202611262040315dc04f09ae834fc0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`test/yang/call/conformance.clj` — a JVM test harness using `clj-comp/read-forms` as the parse for cross-language conformance — since it goes through yang.clojure/read-forms, my change updates it automatically. Good.\n\nNow, let me check the stream_eval_test and callsite_test briefly for relevant structure, then start writing. Actually time is pressing — the biggest risk is the reader implementation and getting both lanes green. Let me get to work.\n\nOrder of operations (respecting TDD + legacy capture):\n1. FIRST capture pre-fix legacy artifacts (before ANY source change): need Node lane built (npm, antlr, yin-repl) + a generator. Do it via a scratch generator namespace + run JVM & Node.\n2. Write RED tests (the seven gates).\n3. RED runs JVM + Node → logs.\n4. Implement.\n5. GREEN JVM + Node.\n6. Dart + Jolt legs.\n7. Docs, re-pin checks, kondo.\n8. Findings.\n\nWait — actually for the legacy artifact generation, simplest is to fold it into the RED test namespace itself: a deftest that, when RUN against pre-fix code, WRITES the fixture files if absent (recording :provenance \"pre-fix\"), and post-fix loads them for custody. Risky (re-running RED after artifacts exist → skip). Cleaner: standalone generator namespace `test/yang/floatkind_legacy_gen.cljc` (not a -test ns so it doesn't auto-run), invoked explicitly:\n- JVM: clojure -M:test -n won't run non-test... use `-v ns/var`? cognitect -v needs var. Or just make it a deftest in its own namespace run once then deleted.\n- Node: node target/node-tests.js --test=<ns> — needs the ns compiled into the build; shadow compiles ALL test namespaces matching ns-regexp (default -test$)?? shadow's node-test auto-discovers namespaces per :ns-regexp?? Default regexp for shadow node-test build — it compiles all test namespaces it finds (from :source-paths matching... hmm). Actually check_node_discovery: \"scan deps.edn :paths + :cljs :extra-paths for .cljc/.cljs namespaces outside test/ matching shadow-cljs.edn :test :ns-regexp (default -test$)\" — so shadow test build includes namespaces ending in -test(-s?). My generator must end in -test to be picked up... or I add ns-regexp? Can't change shadow-cljs.edn (out of bounds? it's not in the boundary list — avoid).\n\nSo: generator namespace yang.clojure-float-kind-legacy-gen-test? No wait — \"matching -test$\" → ns must end with \"-test\". Name: `yang.floatkind-legacy-capture-test`. Run it explicitly via -n (JVM) / --test= (Node) during RED; it writes fixtures + prints provenance; afterwards I DELETE the namespace (it's a one-shot capture tool, not a permanent test). Deleting after capture — but then the fixture-creating code is gone (evidence in logs + findings). That's fine — like the c1-1 fixture whose generator is gone.\n\nHmm, wait — actually there's a subtlety: node-tests.js runs with autorun ALL namespaces? `node target/node-tests.js --test=yang.floatkind-legacy-capture-test` — the --test filter. OK.\n\nBut FIRST the node lane must build: `bb deps:npm` (npm ci), `bb gen:antlr`, `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl` and the test build `... compile test` (which node-tests.js runs). Total first build ~12 min (726s observed). Let me kick off the prerequisite builds NOW in the background while I write tests.\n\nActually — do it in the right order: gen:antlr first (needed by everything), then npm, then yin-repl build, then test build. The task says \"bb gen:antlr first (cache hit expected)\".","signature":"f988edee1141400a83bacf24"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"a37625a7-4e14-4589-a3d1-1fadf6b22c2a","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:40:54.490Z","thinking_duration_ms":16589,"thinking_display":"u