{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_707e19f16aca4f6d87aad4ed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.encoder\n2\t  \"The encoder observer: the `run-on-stream` consumer the composition\n3\t   attaches over the program medium so the semantic VM never sees a map AST\n4\t   or a datom batch (§9.1, `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`).\n5\t\n6\t   It is a stage in its own right, not a loader arm. The composition hands\n7\t   its session the row medium's writer as the consumer; `run-on-stream`\n8\t   hands it each observed program batch; it projects the batch to the\n9\t   canonical row set and forwards it — appends it to the row medium. The\n10\t   evaluator observer the composition attaches to that row medium\n11\t   independently is the next stage: the two never call each other, they\n12\t   communicate through the row medium alone, so compiler and evaluator stay\n13\t   independently attachable (no direct function-to-function coupling\n14\t   without a stream boundary).\n15\t\n16\t   Projection is this boundary's one job (§9.1): the map AST the frontends\n17\t   emit projects directly through `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`; a\n18\t   `:yin/*` datom batch projects through the explicit datom→row adapter\n19\t   below — §7.1's projection path, for media that carry datoms.\"\n20\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n21\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n22\t            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n23\t\n24\t\n25\t(defn source-envelope\n26\t  \"Construct the provenance-bearing input value ruled by D4. The admitting\n27\t   composition supplies its program medium's logical identity and mints a\n28\t   fresh batch token before append. `members` is ordered and `root` selects\n29\t   the member the evaluator runs. The constructor validates but never mints:\n30\t   retries of an unaccepted staged append must retain the caller's token.\"\n31\t  ([source-medium batch-token members]\n32\t   (source-envelope source-medium batch-token members 0))\n33\t  ([source-medium batch-token members root]\n34\t   (let [envelope {:yin/source-medium source-medium\n35\t                   :yin/batch-token batch-token\n36\t                   :yin/batch (vec members)\n37\t                   :yin/root root}]\n38\t     ;; Validating the root origin validates the two opaque coordinates too.\n39\t     (when-not (and (integer? root) (<= 0 root) (< root (count members)))\n40\t       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n41\t                       {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n42\t     (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n43\t     envelope)))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(defn- datom-child-places\n47\t  [get-attr eid]\n48\t  (case (get-attr eid :yin/type)\n49\t    :lambda [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/body)]]\n50\t    :application (concat [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/operator)]]\n51\t                         (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n52\t                                      (get-attr eid :yin/operands)))\n53\t    :if [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/test)]\n54\t         [3 (get-attr eid :yin/consequent)]\n55\t         [4 (get-attr eid :yin/alternate)]]\n56\t    :dao.stream.apply/call\n57\t    (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n58\t                 (get-attr eid :yin/operands))\n59\t    :stream/put [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/target)]\n60\t                 [3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"800c468d-5d15-40c3-be38-46b077b0ecfc","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:41:49.412Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.encoder\n  \"The encoder observer: the `run-on-stream` consumer the composition\n   attaches over the program medium so the semantic VM never sees a map AST\n   or a datom batch (§9.1, `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`).\n\n   It is a stage in its own right, not a loader arm. The composition hands\n   its session the row medium's writer as the consumer; `run-on-stream`\n   hands it each observed program batch; it projects the batch to the\n   canonical row set and forwards it — appends it to the row medium. The\n   evaluator observer the composition attaches to that row medium\n   independently is the next stage: the two never call each other, they\n   communicate through the row medium alone, so compiler and evaluator stay\n   independently attachable (no direct function-to-function coupling\n   without a stream boundary).\n\n   Projection is this boundary's one job (§9.1): the map AST the frontends\n   emit projects directly through `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`; a\n   `:yin/*` datom batch projects through the explicit datom→row adapter\n   below — §7.1's projection path, for media that carry datoms.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn source-envelope\n  \"Construct the provenance-bearing input value ruled by D4. The admitting\n   composition supplies its program medium's logical identity and mints a\n   fresh batch token before append. `members` is ordered and `root` selects\n   the member the evaluator runs. The constructor validates but never mints:\n   retries of an unaccepted staged append must retain the caller's token.\"\n  ([source-medium batch-token members]\n   (source-envelope source-medium batch-token members 0))\n  ([source-medium batch-token members root]\n   (let [envelope {:yin/source-medium source-medium\n                   :yin/batch-token batch-token\n                   :yin/batch (vec members)\n                   :yin/root root}]\n     ;; Validating the root origin validates the two opaque coordinates too.\n     (when-not (and (integer? root) (<= 0 root) (< root (count members)))\n       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n                       {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n     (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n     envelope)))\n\n\n(defn- datom-child-places\n  [get-attr eid]\n  (case (get-attr eid :yin/type)\n    :lambda [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/body)]]\n    :application (concat [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/operator)]]\n                         (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n                                      (get-attr eid :yin/operands)))\n    :if [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/test)]\n         [3 (get-attr eid :yin/consequent)]\n         [4 (get-attr eid :yin/alternate)]]\n    :dao.stream.apply/call\n    (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n                 (get-attr eid :yin/operands))\n    :stream/put [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/target)]\n                 [3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":451}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_707e19f16aca4f6d87aad4ed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
