{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026112620450293b898c55e2045fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Problem: `(exists? \"cljs.core\")` — exists? is a cljs macro checking a name... In cljs `(exists? \"cljs.core\")` checks global var — this runs on :clj too where exists? doesn't exist! Need reader conditionals mid-line. Also jvm-write! references clojure.java.io which isn't required on :cljs... The :clj branch code compiles only if the reader conditional includes it. Let me rewrite the whole file once more, carefully, using mid-line `#?(:clj ... :cljs ...)`.\n\nThe shell guard rejects \"newline followed by #\" INSIDE THE QUOTED ARG — so as long as `#?` never immediately follows a newline, fine. Let me compose the final version in one python write with everything correct:\n\n- ns require: clojure.test, dao.jing, dao.jing.cbor, yang.clojure, yin.vm. On :clj also clojure.java.io — put in ns :require via reader conditional — must be mid-line: `(:require [clojure.test ...] #?(:clj [clojure.java.io :as io]) ...)`. Hmm — `#?@` splicing mid-line is fine.\n- host detection: `(defn- cljs-build? [] #?(:clj false :cljs true))` — one line each.\n- write: `(defn- write-bytes! [path payload] (let [bytes (cbor/encode payload)] #?(:clj (do (io/make-parents path) (with-open [w (io/output-stream path)] (.write w ^bytes bytes))) :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path bytes)) bytes))`.\n\nWrite the full final file.","signature":"acf2c11e67e94c6b97118ac0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"dc79c19e-76bd-417f-b484-03b430611db0","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:45:11.274Z","thinking_duration_ms":6600,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026112620450293b898c55e2045fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_0a17b04cbb1c470eb7893493","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c 'import pathlib\npathlib.Path(\"test/yang/floatkind_legacy_capture_test.cljc\").write_text(\"\"\"(ns yang.floatkind-legacy-capture-test\n  \\\"\\\"\\\"ONE-SHOT pre-fix evidence capture (float-kind portability r1, RULING 5\n   gate 6): mints the legacy custody fixtures from the CURRENT compiler —\n   the JVM float-bearing artifact and the Node integer-bearing artifact of\n   the SAME source — and writes them under test/resources/yang/clojure/.\n\n   Run once on each host against the UNREPAIRED tree, then delete this\n   namespace. The fixtures it leaves behind are the genuine pre-fix bytes\n   the custody test loads and executes without recompilation afterwards;\n   an artifact synthesized by the repaired compiler would not be legacy\n   evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            #?(:clj [clojure.java.io :as io])))\n\n\n(def ^:private legacy-source\n  \\\"\\\"\\\"The custody witness program: a float literal under a closure call.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n  \\\"((fn [] 1.0))\\\")\n\n\n(defn- host-of [] #?(:clj :jvm-float :cljs :node-integer :default :other))\n\n\n(defn- write-bytes!\n  [path payload]\n  (let [bytes (cbor/encode payload)]\n    #?(:clj (do (io/make-parents path)\n                (with-open [w (io/output-stream path)]\n                  (.write w ^bytes bytes)))\n       :cljs (.writeFileSync (js/require \\\"fs\\\") path bytes))\n    bytes))\n\n\n(deftest capture-legacy-float-kind-artifact\n  (let [ast (yang/compile-program (yang/read-forms legacy-source))\n        tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n        host (host-of)\n        payload {:yang.clojure.floatkind/legacy true\n                 :yang.clojure.floatkind/host host\n                 :yang.clojure.floatkind/source legacy-source\n                 :yang.clojure.floatkind/pre-fix-ref \\\"7f4898f4 c1-2\\\"\n                 :manifest-revision \\\"c1-2\\\"\n                 :root (:root tree)\n                 :rows (:rows tree)}\n        path (str \\\"test/resources/yang/clojure/float-kind-legacy-\\\"\n                  (name host) \\\".cbor\\\")\n        bytes (write-bytes! path payload)]\n    (println :floatkind-legacy-capture host :bytes (count bytes))\n    (is (pos? (count bytes)))))\n\"\"\")'","description":"Write final capture namespace"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"56752cc3-e6c5-4d7d-b8a8-24a1df5b6762","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:45:16.465Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call_0a17b04cbb1c470eb7893493":{"command":"python3 -c 'import pathlib\npathlib.Path(\"test/yang/floatkind_legacy_capture_test.cljc\").write_text(\"\"\"(ns yang.floatkind-legacy-capture-test\n  \\\"\\\"\\\"ONE-SHOT pre-fix evidence capture (float-kind portability r1, RULING 5\n   gate 6): mints the legacy custody fixtures from the CURRENT compiler —\n   the JVM float-bearing artifact and the Node integer-bearing artifact of\n   the SAME source — and writes them under test/resources/yang/clojure/.\n\n   Run once on each host against the UNREPAIRED tree, then delete this\n   namespace. The fixtures it leaves behind are the genuine pre-fix bytes\n   the custody test loads and executes without recompilation afterwards;\n   an artifact synthesized by the repaired compiler would not be legacy\n   evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            #?(:clj [clojure.java.io