te (no opts) — `inc` free symbol → native? no convention → variable → runtime lookup in :primitives... vm/primitives has 'inc? Let me check — earlier core_impl inc is the GUEST library (clojure.core.impl). In the plain REPL route, is inc in vm/primitives? grep later. If inc resolves to host inc: JVM (inc 1.0-Double) → 2.0 Double → float64? true (JVM passes); Node (inc 1) → 2 → false → RED. Post-fix Node: 1.0 → carrier → host inc on carrier → JS inc carrier → NaN/coercion issue → adapter needed... my numeric override set: + - * comparisons — inc/dec are NOT in vm/primitives probably (they're core_impl). In the REPL default route without the library... hmm — what does \"(inc 1)\" do in the REPL today? It must work — inc must be resolvable. vm/primitives — let me grep for 'inc entry.","signature":"7b93cb786f314a32a3c21ca0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"45fdf7e0-6972-4b7e-b55e-f1365d0003d7","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:47:52.132Z","thinking_duration_ms":34883,"thinking_display":"updates"}
