{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126204811473fac2c039b4ead","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Very interesting current REPL behavior (JVM, pre-fix):\n- `(inc 1.0)` → ERROR \"Unable to resolve symbol: inc\" — inc is NOT available in the plain REPL route (it's the guest library's, only under the linked/outcome convention). So gate 4's inc/dec tests must run through the LINKED/library route (compile-program with unit-opts / the outcome lane like the corpus test's run-outcome with :outcomes true + the library?). The corpus `run-outcome` used outcome-opts with `:native (set (keys vm/primitives))` — but not the library modules... yet gate 4 says \"In the selected Clojure library profile, inc/dec of floating input must take floating behavior\". The \"selected Clojure library profile\" = the linked runtime (clj module) — like lower-unit programs run via clj/run-main. How do existing tests exercise the library profile? Let me find a test that runs with the clojure library (clojure.core.impl) — maybe test/yang/clojure_test.clj or call/conformance. Search for run-main/lower-unit tests.\n- `(+ 1.5 1.5)` → \"3.0\" text — works, JVM Double.\n- `1.0` → \"1.0\" text.\n- `(assoc {} 1.0 :a)` → \"{1.0 :a}\" — NO refusal on JVM! Because constant 1.0 → hmm, `(assoc {} 1.0 :a)` — assoc application → runtime collection-assoc (vm/primitives 'assoc) → host assoc with Double key — no clj/collection-key policy in the plain route (that's the clj runtime's impl-assoc). So float-key refusal only applies under the library profile. The ruling: \"Where float keys/elements are prohibited by a profile, require the same explicit refusal on both hosts\" — profile-scoped. In the library profile, (assoc {} 1.0 :a) → clj/collection-key → :coll/unsupported-key policy. In the plain REPL route there's no such policy — existing behavior. Gate 4: \"Verify integer key admission versus floating refusal, including nested key Data and guest collection-policy behavior.\" — under the library profile. And for the plain profile... data/admit-key? direct (host-level oracle).\n\nSo I need to find how tests run programs under the library profile. Look at call/conformance.clj :clojure — it publishes clj runtime and runs lower-unit via run-main. That's the JVM conformance harness. Is there a lighter path — `yang.clojure/lower-unit` + linker run? Let me look for existing tests using unit-opts or lower-unit.","signature":"5d2ec652de224798bd8927a7"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"4697c5f7-9c2d-47ef-be85-6024bb0bcc79","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:48:26.491Z","thinking_duration_ms":10842,"thinking_display":"updates"}
