fmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n1997\t   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n1998\t   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n1999\t   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n2000\t   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n2001\t  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n2002\t  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n2003\t  ([forms tail? opts]\n2004\t   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n2005\t   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n2006\t     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n2007\t     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n2008\t     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles its\n2009\t     ;; paths at each definition during machine-data validation and UCF lift."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"14a6476b-eb9a-4205-a813-bf774ffdf1be","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:48:57.552Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc","content":"        (when-not (symbol? head)\n          (check-program-symbols! head))\n        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\n    (map? form) (run! check-program-symbols! (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n    (coll? form) (run! check-program-symbols! form)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-top-form\n  \"A non-definition top-level expression lowers like a function body (plain\n   values, `throw`/`try` onto the continuation family); definitions keep\n   their own lowering.\"\n  [env macro-env form]\n  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n    form\n    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n\n\n(defn- with-runtime\n  \"Wrap a unit in its clj entry boundary and initialize the needed core exports.\"\n  [