{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126205234b9413a54acd2483b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait — issue: gate4 tests use `repl-session-result` which is only defined under #?(:clj ...)/#?(:cljs ...) — on :cljd/:jolt those deftests referencing it won't compile. Need the gate 2/4 REPL deftests gated too. Also `read-one \"'{:a [1.0]}\"` — `get-in` on a map by :a key: (get-in '(quote {:a [1.0]}) [1 :a 0]) — [1 :a 0]: (nth form 1) = the map, then :a, then 0. get-in with keywords on lists? get-in uses get — (get map :a) fine, (get vector 0) fine, (get list 1) — get on a list returns nil for index! get-in [2 0 1] on '(let [x 1.0] x): (get '(let ...) 2) — get on a LIST is nil!! Must use nth for seqs. Fix positions helper to use nth-based navigation. Let me fix: for list forms use (nth form 2). I'll rewrite that block with explicit nth calls.\n\nAlso `(read-one \"(quote [1.0 1])\")` — quote form '(quote [1.0 1]): (nth 1) = the vector. And \"'{:a [1.0]}\" → (quote {:a [1.0]}) → (nth 1) = map → (:a m) → (nth v 0).\n\nAlso — `\\\\1` char literal: my python string had \"\\\\\\\\1\" → file contains `\\\\1` → Clojure string \"\\\\1\" → the reader sees source \"\\\\1\"?? Wait the TEST does (read-one \"\\\\1\") — the Clojure string literal \"\\\\1\" IS the 2-char string \\1 — read-one receives source \"\\1\" (backslash + 1) → our reader → char \\1. Expected (= \\1 result). In my part I wrote `(is (= 42 (read-one \"1.0 #_ (+ 1.0 2.0) 42\")))` — fine. But I dropped the char test in the rewrite? I see \"string content\", \"comment skipped\", discards — I removed the char line in part a? Yes I removed it (good — char representation is host-specific: JVM Character vs cljs string — (= \\1 result) would compare Character vs string on cljs → false! Actually on cljs \\1 IS \"1\"-ish string — read returns \"1\"? cljs chars are strings of len 1. (read-one \"\\\\1\") cljs → \"1\"? and \\1 in cljs test code is also \"1\". So (= \\1 ...) works on cljs; on JVM Character. Both fine actually — but host representation differences make it a weak test; keep it out — already out.)\n\nNow fix the positions navigation and add gate 5/6/7. Also gate2-macro / gate4-repl deftests must be host-gated. Let me patch positions with nth.","signature":"1dab2a5d16894ffabe41f70b"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"461c8a46-32d7-451e-97de-0f3d5c2ca954","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:52:52.003Z","thinking_duration_ms":13357,"thinking_display":"updates"}
