{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126205304bd9a9c2558f44f52","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"That approach is broken — I can't just prefix `#?(:clj (` without closing. Since the REPL helpers are only defined on :clj/:cljs, and the whole namespace must LOAD on :cljd (Dart leg), the cleanest is: define no-op stubs of repl-session-result/repl-text/repl-error? on :cljd/:jolt so the deftests compile but... they'd call the stub → fail. Better: gate with a `(def ^:private repl-supported? #?(:clj true :cljs true :default false))` and wrap the BODIES: `(when repl-supported? (testing ...))` — deftests exist everywhere but skip on cljd/jolt. But bodies still reference the vars — vars must EXIST on cljd. So define the helpers on :default hosts as `(defn- repl-session-result [_] (throw ...))`? Then when repl-supported? false → not called. Clean enough. Let me revert the staging and restructure: single helper definitions with #? conditional bodies.\n\nSimplest: replace the two #?(:clj (do ...)) #?(:cljs (do ...)) blocks with ONE block:\n\n```cljc\n(def ^:private repl-route? #?(:clj true :cljs true :default false))\n\n#?(:clj (require ...))  ; already in ns\n```\nand define the fns for :default as stubs via:\n```cljc\n(defn- repl-session-result\n  [line]\n  #?(:clj (repl-result-impl line)\n     :cljs (repl-result-impl line)\n     :default (throw (ex-info \"no REPL route on this host\" {}))))\n```\nwith repl-result-impl defined similarly host-gated... but repl-result-impl would itself reference repl/frontends — same problem one level down; but reader conditionals INSIDE a defn body only compile the taken branch — YES! `#?(:clj ...)` inside a defn body — the reader conditional is processed at READ time, so the :cljd branch never sees the repl/ vars. So:\n\n```cljc\n(defn- repl-session-result [line]\n  (let [[state _] (#?(:clj repl/eval-input :cljs repl/eval-input :default nil)\n                   ...)])\n```\nHmm — messy inline. Cleaner: the whole let body in one branch:\n\n```cljc\n(defn- repl-session-result\n  [line]\n  #?(:clj (let [[state _] (repl/eval-input (frontends/create-state {:vm-type :semantic}) line)] (drain-result state))\n     :cljs (let [[state _] (repl/eval-input (frontends/create-state {:vm-type :semantic}) line)] (drain-result state))\n     :default nil))\n```\nwith drain-result a plain fn over the output stream (no host deps — stream API is portable). And repl-text similar. Then deftests wrap assertions in (when repl-route? ...). Let me rewrite the helper section wholesale.","signature":"1b06df4773254ee7aa27aa21"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"a48d7bf6-2958-43b2-aeba-cf03bf64a720","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:53:18.391Z","thinking_duration_ms":11196,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261126205304bd9a9c2558f44f52","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_805420be3d06405688a1f61e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport pathlib, re\np = pathlib.Path(\"test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc\")\nt = p.read_text()\n# revert the broken #?(:clj (deftest staging\nt = t.replace(\"#?(:clj (deftest \", \"(deftest \")\n# replace the whole helper block between the host-read-file defn and GATE 1 marker\nstart = t.index(\"(defn- host-read-file\")\nend = t.index(\";; =============================================================================\\n;; GATE 1\")\nhelpers = '''(defn- host-read-file\n  [path]\n  #?(:clj (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath (io/file path)))\n     :cljs (.readFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path)\n     :default nil))\n\n\n(def ^:private repl-route?\n  \"The REPL/catalog route runs where the shell runs; the Dart and Jolt legs\n  of this namespace exercise artifacts and capability claims only.\"\n  #?(:clj true :cljs true :default false))\n\n\n(defn- drain-result\n  \"The :repl/result value of a shell's output medium, oldest first.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [output (:output-stream state)\n        cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor output :dao.stream/oldest))]\n    (loop [cursor cursor, value ::none]\n      (let [step (stream/next output cursor)]\n        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome step))\n          (let [v (:dao.stream/value step)]\n            (if (= :repl/result (:type v))\n              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor step) (:value v))\n              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor step) value)))\n          value)))))\n\n\n(defn- repl-session-result\n  \"The result value of evaluating `line` through the standard REPL/catalog\n  route (the frontends the shell installs), semantic VM.\"\n  [line]\n  #?(:clj (drain-result (first (repl/eval-input (frontends/create-state {:vm-type :semantic}) line)))\n     :cljs 