{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_e43e8fdd7ad046348ce2ff91","type":"tool_result","content":"15:            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n122:(deftest ^:slow pure-expressions-and-let-bindings-evaluate-on-every-vm\n153:(deftest a-program-makes-writes-and-reads-a-stream-in-one-round\n168:(deftest ^:slow a-stream-is-ingested-transformed-and-emitted-across-rounds\n203:(deftest a-cursor-is-one-readers-progress\n220:(deftest a-full-ring-evicts-its-oldest-element\n233:(deftest a-closed-stream-refuses-writes-and-ends-reads\n256:(deftest a-read-on-an-empty-stream-parks-and-the-round-is-consumed\n266:            [_ parked next-round put after] results\n268:        (is (error? parked)\n270:        (is (str/includes? parked \"runnable\"))\n273:            \"the stream outlives the parked round; a later read succeeds\")\n282:(deftest output-and-results-are-emitted-on-the-output-medium\n305:(deftest programs-are-ingested-as-batches-on-the-program-media\n337:(deftest a-session-threads-definitions-streams-and-history\n359:(deftest reset-and-vm-selection-forget-streams-with-the-session\n380:(deftest multi-line-input-accumulates-a-stream-program\n417:(deftest ^:slow every-vm-answers-the-same-stream-script\n(ns yang.clojure.stream-eval-test\n  \"yang.clojure stream programs on yin.vm, evaluated through the yin.repl\n   shell, which is the composition around dao.stream media: each program\n   is compiled by yang.clojure, appended to the program medium as one row\n   batch, expanded onto the row medium, loaded and run by the evaluator's\n   observer, and answered on the output medium as printed chunks followed\n   by one result token (yin.repl; docs/design/dao.stream.md).  The streams\n   a program makes -- `stream/make`, `put!`, `cursor`, `next!`, `close!`\n   -- are ring buffers the shell hands the VM as `:make-stream`, so every\n   stream a program touches is a dao.stream medium.\n\n   Every case runs on the four evaluators the shell composes, with the\n   value texts pinned, so the cases double as a cross-VM parity corpus.\"\n  (:require [dao.test-slow :as slow] [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Harness\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def vm-types\n  \"Every evaluator the shell composes (`yin.repl/vm-constructors`).\"\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- session\n  \"A fresh shell on `vm-type`, optionally around a caller-owned output\n   medium.\"\n  ([vm-type] (session vm-type nil))\n  ([vm-type output]\n   (repl.frontends/create-state (cond-> {:vm-type vm-type}\n                                  output (assoc :output-stream output)))))\n\n\n(defn- evaluate","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a","uuid":"098ad794-07bd-48ea-ada0-c274f228f02c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T12:55:28.110Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"15:            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n122:(deftest ^:slow pure-expressions-and-let-bindings-evaluate-on-every-vm\n153:(deftest a-program-makes-writes-and-reads-a-stream-in-one-round\n168:(deftest ^:slow a-stream-is-ingested-transformed-and-emitted-across-rounds\n203:(deftest a-cursor-is-one-readers-progress\n220:(deftest a-full-ring-evicts-its-oldest-element\n233:(deftest a-closed-stream-refuses-writes-and-ends-reads\n256:(deftest a-read-on-an-empty-stream-parks-and-the-round-is-consumed\n266:            [_ parked next-round put after] results\n268:        (is (error? parked)\n270:        (is (str/includes? parked \"runnable\"))\n273:            \"the stream outlives the parked round; a later read succeeds\")\n282:(deftest output-and-results-are-emitted-on-the-output-medium\n305:(deftest programs-are-ingested-as-batches-on-the-program-media\n337:(deftest a-session-threads-definitions-streams-and-history\n359:(deftest reset-and-vm-selection-forget-streams-with-the-session\n380:(deftest multi-line-input-accumulates-a-stream-program\n417:(deftest ^:slow every-vm-answers-the-same-stream-script\n(ns yang.clojure.stream-eval-test\n  \"yang.clojure stream programs on yin.vm, evaluated through the yin.repl\n   shell, which is the composition around dao.stream media: each program\n   is compiled by yang.clojure, appended to the program medium as one row\n   batch, expanded onto the row medium, loaded and run by the evaluator's\n   observer, and answered on the output medium as printed chunks followed\n   by one result token (yin.repl; docs/design/dao.stream.md).  The streams\n   a program makes -- `stream/make`, `put!`, `cursor`, `next!`, `close!`\n   -- are ring buffers the shell hands the VM as `:make-stream`, so every\n   stream a program touches is a dao.stream medium.\n\n   Every case runs on the four evaluators the shell composes, with the\n   value texts pinned, so the cases double as a cross-VM parity corpus.\"\n  (:require [dao.test-slow :as slow] [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n            [yin.repl :as repl]\n            [yin.repl.frontends :as repl.frontends]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Harness\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def vm-types\n  \"Every evaluator the shell composes (`yin.repl/vm-constructors`).\"\n  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- session\n  \"A fresh shell on `vm-type`, optionally around a caller-owned output\n   medium.\"\n  ([vm-type] (session vm-type nil))\n  ([vm-type output]\n   (repl.frontends/create-state (cond-> {:vm-type vm-type}\n                                  output (assoc :output-stream output)))))\n\n\n(defn- evaluate","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_e43e8fdd7ad046348ce2ff91","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
